<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aleksandras Stulginskis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1885">1885</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aleksandras Stulginskis was a Lithuanian Christian Democrat politician who chaired the Constituent Assembly from 1920 and served as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1920 to 1926, overseeing land reform and the 1922 constitution. After the Soviet occupation he was deported to a labour camp in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> in 1941 and returned to Lithuania only in 1956.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aleksandras-stulginskis.jpg" alt="Aleksandras Stulginskis" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aleksandras_Stulginskis_(1885-1969).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
